@ Besides the stage and the vectors that the accessors expose, the scene
keeps the time at which the stage is sampled, the index from paths to meshes,
and two caches that we shall explain with the materials: a material is
converted only once however many prims bind it, and a texture is decoded only
once however many materials read it. Materials and textures refer to each
other, and meshes to materials, by their indices in these vectors.

